The  utility is a time server daemon which is normally invoked at
boot time from the file.  It synchronizes the  host’s  time  with
the  time  of  other  machines, which are also running in a local
area network.  These time servers will slow down  the  clocks  of
some  machines and speed up the clocks of others to bring them to
the average network time.  The average network time  is  computed
from  measurements  of  clock differences using the timestamp re‐
quest message.  The following options are available:  Enable  de‐
