When  is started on a machine, it asks the master for the network
time and sets the host’s clock to that time.  After that, it  ac‐
cepts  synchronization  messages  periodically sent by the master
and calls to perform the needed corrections on the host’s  clock.
It  also communicates with in order to set the date globally, and
with a control utility.  If the machine running  the  master  be‐
comes  unreachable, the slaves will elect a new master from among
those slaves which are running with  at  least  one  of  the  and
